  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round1_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B041",
        "laureates": [
          "Christopher Jarzynski",
          "Denis J. Evans",
          "Giovanni Gallavotti"
        ],
        "citation": "for fluctuation theorems linking irreversibility, work, and equilibrium free energies far from equilibrium"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B013",
    "B034"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B041 identifies a clean and unusually universal physical mechanism: probabilistic fluctuations in entropy production and work obey exact constraints even away from equilibrium. Evans and Gallavotti established a seminal fluctuation relation, while Jarzynski supplied the equality that makes nonequilibrium work a route to equilibrium free-energy differences. The results have become experimentally and theoretically useful across molecular, soft-matter, and quantum systems, with a maturity that does not depend on one prospective technology succeeding.",
    "case_against": "The candidate groups several closely related relations rather than one discrete discovery, and the historical division between the fluctuation theorem and the Jarzynski equality must be framed precisely. Its breadth is also a reservation: wide use across systems should not substitute for establishing a single prize-defining experimental breakthrough.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson argues that dynamical mean-field theory is mature, broadly tested, and provides a bridge from many-body theory to spectroscopy and electronic-structure calculations, while noting that it is an approximation.",
        "response": "I agree that B013 is an exceptionally influential and mature framework, and it remains my strongest alternative. But the approximation caveat is material: its great value is as a controlled and productive method, whereas B041 states general relations that reorganize the physical meaning of fluctuations and dissipation. I therefore retain B041 ahead of B013."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll emphasizes that optical lattice clocks combine Katori's magic-wavelength concept with Ye's foundational experimental advances and have been independently reproduced at extraordinary precision.",
        "response": "The attribution for B034 is admirably compact and the metrological achievement is beyond dispute. I nevertheless qualify its priority here because the most consequential applications and any redefinition of the second are still evolving. B041 has already supplied a durable conceptual law and a broad body of tests, rather than chiefly an exceptionally capable measurement architecture."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson regards quantum error correction as the foundational answer to decoherence and scalable quantum information processing, while recognizing that full fault-tolerant computation remains incomplete.",
        "response": "I share the judgment that B003 isolates a fundamental mechanism and that the three proposed contributors have distinct roles. The unresolved demonstration of fault tolerance at consequential scale is, however, central rather than incidental. It leaves B003 behind B041 at present, though ahead of many technology-led candidates."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the prize citation can unite the Evans-Gallavotti relation and Jarzynski equality without blurring their distinct historical formulations",
      "Whether the experimental record is sufficiently decisive to make a broadly applicable theoretical relation the preferred physics prize"
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
